From 90750c0e68228f7c0feb883dc3ec280e9e5df801 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Manrique <125496885+hashd1ve@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 13:11:49 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] feat(dsv41): prompts with images keep and resume their
 prompt states, matched by the images' digests

A prompt with images ran whole on every turn and kept nothing: the cache matched tokens, and an image's span is its
placeholder token repeated, the same for every image. An agent session with a few screenshots then prefilled its whole
history at each turn (73K tokens, ~40 s on two GB10s), and the other streams waited.

The server now gives the request a cache key: the prompt's ids with each image span spelled by its image's digest (one
id a position, past every vocabulary), and the history length past the spans. The lane host looks up, keeps and reports
under that key, and the dsv41 lanes resume and keep prompt states whatever images the prompt holds: a state the key
matched holds the same images' rows. A prompt with another image at the same span matches only before it.

Tests: the lane host resumes a prompt with an image past it when its key matches and not when the image differs
(fails before this change: nothing is looked up for a prompt with images); the key's ids depend on the image and the
position and stay past the vocabulary.
